1
00:01:16,105 --> 00:01:16,563
Die, idiot

2
00:01:17,105 --> 00:01:17,438
Die

3
00:01:25,355 --> 00:01:25,895
Bro

4
00:01:25,896 --> 00:01:27,688
he's not telling when
he'll return the money, Bro

5
00:01:29,105 --> 00:01:32,230
It's my habit to pray
before committing a sin

6
00:01:35,980 --> 00:01:37,271
Where's my money, huh?

7
00:01:37,980 --> 00:01:38,438
Daivaji

8
00:01:39,271 --> 00:01:39,855
please let me go!

9
00:01:40,771 --> 00:01:41,730
I'll return your money

10
00:01:42,313 --> 00:01:42,855
Don't kill me

11
00:01:43,813 --> 00:01:44,521
Hey,

12
00:01:44,896 --> 00:01:46,688
do you remember the story
of the cow and the tiger?

13
00:01:46,980 --> 00:01:49,521
In that story,
the tiger gave the cow one chance

14
00:01:49,813 --> 00:01:51,980
I gave you two chances

15
00:01:52,355 --> 00:01:55,855
The principal and interest
together come to twenty-five lakhs

16
00:01:56,188 --> 00:01:58,313
You kept saying you'd pay,

17
00:01:58,771 --> 00:02:00,896
then locked up your house and ran away.

18
00:02:01,146 --> 00:02:03,021
I worked hard to find you

19
00:02:04,396 --> 00:02:05,730
and now you're saying the same thing again

20
00:02:06,521 --> 00:02:08,105
Did you think the tiger would trust you?

21
00:02:08,688 --> 00:02:10,688
Did you think the
tiger would let you live?

22
00:02:12,980 --> 00:02:16,313
Killing someone is a
greater sin than make to kill

23
00:02:17,146 --> 00:02:19,146
I'm sure I'm going to hell

24
00:02:19,646 --> 00:02:20,187
What do you say?

25
00:02:20,188 --> 00:02:20,980
[Chuckles]

26
00:02:21,146 --> 00:02:21,646
Yes, Boss

27
00:02:22,021 --> 00:02:24,188
You laugh when I say
I'm going to hell, huh?

28
00:02:24,355 --> 00:02:25,479
Idiots!

29
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:26,271
Hey! Janaki

30
00:02:26,521 --> 00:02:26,938
Yes, Boss

31
00:02:28,855 --> 00:02:31,896
Pack it up. Take the money
and send these fools away urgently.

32
00:02:32,146 --> 00:02:33,438
I can't bear to look
at their pathetic faces

33
00:03:10,688 --> 00:03:11,188
Come

34
00:03:11,688 --> 00:03:13,563
I came here because
I couldn't refuse you, Dad

35
00:03:14,188 --> 00:03:15,521
But I won't come inside

36
00:03:16,230 --> 00:03:17,646
Just the thought of seeing that idiot...

37
00:03:19,355 --> 00:03:20,563
You just go and come back quickly

38
00:03:26,438 --> 00:03:26,813
Hmm

39
00:03:30,688 --> 00:03:32,063
Sprinkle turmeric water all over the house

40
00:03:32,771 --> 00:03:35,063
A misfortune worse than
corpse has stepped into this home

41
00:03:40,688 --> 00:03:41,896
How long will you keep up this anger?

42
00:03:42,188 --> 00:03:43,105
I'm your father!

43
00:03:43,230 --> 00:03:43,855
Hey, stop it!

44
00:03:45,146 --> 00:03:47,938
If you say that word again,
I'll rip the nerve out of your throat!

45
00:03:48,813 --> 00:03:50,230
Our Bhanu is getting married

46
00:03:50,688 --> 00:03:52,021
I just wanted to let you know...

47
00:03:55,146 --> 00:03:57,563
Let me know or to insult me?

48
00:03:59,438 --> 00:04:01,479
You shamelessly became
the man of this house twice,

49
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:02,480
and now you're making him.

50
00:04:03,021 --> 00:04:05,229
I remarried for your sake

51
00:04:05,230 --> 00:04:06,521
can't you understand that?

52
00:04:06,688 --> 00:04:07,355
Ugh... disgusting

53
00:04:08,605 --> 00:04:10,229
You remarried to satisfy your lust,

54
00:04:10,230 --> 00:04:13,105
and now you're pretending
it was to uplift your son?

55
00:04:14,521 --> 00:04:15,938
Disgusting... Look at your pathetic life!

56
00:04:18,021 --> 00:04:19,021
How dare you spit on father!

57
00:04:19,646 --> 00:04:20,854
I'll kill you, scoundrel!

58
00:04:20,855 --> 00:04:22,271
Hey, stop! I said stop!

59
00:04:22,730 --> 00:04:23,688
He is my elder son!

60
00:04:24,021 --> 00:04:26,771
As long as I live, you have to give
him the respect as he is elder brother

61
00:04:27,063 --> 00:04:27,771
Calm down!

62
00:04:29,730 --> 00:04:32,730
How dare to come to my
house and give me a warning?

63
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:38,230
If you don't step out right now,
two more packed bundles will go out.

64
00:04:39,105 --> 00:04:39,730
Get out!

65
00:04:44,146 --> 00:04:44,771
Come, Dad

66
00:04:50,646 --> 00:04:51,188
Ugh

67
00:04:52,355 --> 00:04:53,605
[Cell phone rings]

68
00:05:16,896 --> 00:05:18,605
[Cell phone rings]

69
00:05:20,021 --> 00:05:22,896
[Rap lines]

70
00:07:00,646 --> 00:07:00,896
Hey

71
00:07:01,813 --> 00:07:04,104
whoever did this has completely
destroyed everything!

72
00:07:04,105 --> 00:07:04,729
Hey

73
00:07:04,730 --> 00:07:06,855
the windows, doors, and furniture
everything's been smashed to pieces!

74
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:09,063
Nothing else is left here, man

75
00:07:09,688 --> 00:07:10,563
What do we do now?

76
00:07:13,105 --> 00:07:13,688
Come, let's ask

77
00:07:13,813 --> 00:07:14,605
Hey, where's the SI?

78
00:07:14,980 --> 00:07:15,396
Where's the pen?

79
00:07:16,063 --> 00:07:16,812
Where's the paper?
- [Cup shatters]

80
00:07:16,813 --> 00:07:17,604
We should file a complaint

81
00:07:17,605 --> 00:07:19,688
Who is the SI here?

82
00:07:20,188 --> 00:07:20,895
Writer is here

83
00:07:20,896 --> 00:07:22,230
The culprits need to be arrested urgently

84
00:07:22,438 --> 00:07:23,313
We need justice

85
00:07:23,521 --> 00:07:25,813
These guys seem to have downed
a couple of pegs more than me

86
00:07:26,105 --> 00:07:27,312
Hey buffalo, come here

87
00:07:27,313 --> 00:07:27,938
Silence!

88
00:07:28,313 --> 00:07:29,021
You three, come here

89
00:07:29,688 --> 00:07:31,313
Hey, he might be the writer. Come
Hmm... let's go

90
00:07:31,855 --> 00:07:32,480
Hey

91
00:07:33,021 --> 00:07:34,021
I think this is the SI

92
00:07:34,813 --> 00:07:35,438
Put the truncheon down

93
00:07:36,146 --> 00:07:36,855
Hi, sir

94
00:07:37,980 --> 00:07:38,729
Hey

95
00:07:38,730 --> 00:07:41,063
what's with that truncheon
and those get-ups?

96
00:07:41,896 --> 00:07:42,646
What's the issue?

97
00:07:42,855 --> 00:07:44,480
Is it wrong for us to
work for our dreams, sir?

98
00:07:44,980 --> 00:07:46,730
We believed in our dreams
and ended up broke, sir

99
00:07:47,230 --> 00:07:48,729
We should not read
someone else's history, sir

100
00:07:48,730 --> 00:07:50,730
Everyone should read our history.
Is that wrong, sir?

101
00:07:51,063 --> 00:07:51,730
Tell us, sir

102
00:07:51,938 --> 00:07:52,605
Hey

103
00:07:52,730 --> 00:07:55,145
I'm holding my head
here with all this nonsense

104
00:07:55,146 --> 00:07:55,896
What exactly happened?

105
00:07:56,021 --> 00:07:57,980
Someone demolished
our company overnight, sir.

106
00:07:58,146 --> 00:07:58,854
Which company?

107
00:07:58,855 --> 00:07:59,646
The Smash Room

108
00:08:00,188 --> 00:08:01,480
Smash it - Destroy it, sir

109
00:08:01,605 --> 00:08:01,980
What?

110
00:08:02,146 --> 00:08:03,187
Is it flour mill?

111
00:08:03,188 --> 00:08:05,855
Do you call such a prestigious
company as a flour mill?

112
00:08:06,313 --> 00:08:07,271
You should be ashamed, sir.

113
00:08:07,438 --> 00:08:10,480
This is the finest...
Oh, you bloody idiot...

114
00:08:10,730 --> 00:08:11,438
What's your name?

115
00:08:11,688 --> 00:08:12,480
Call me Pammu

116
00:08:12,896 --> 00:08:13,605
Pammu...

117
00:08:14,521 --> 00:08:16,437
Pammu... Pappi... Bujji...

118
00:08:16,438 --> 00:08:17,396
Why are you naming dogs?

119
00:08:17,813 --> 00:08:18,438
Tell me your full name.

120
00:08:19,730 --> 00:08:21,520
Gali Parameshwara Rao, sir

121
00:08:21,521 --> 00:08:22,521
That's better, you donkey

122
00:08:23,563 --> 00:08:24,230
What's your name?

123
00:08:24,396 --> 00:08:24,813
Mano, sir.

124
00:08:25,355 --> 00:08:26,188
Full name

125
00:08:26,855 --> 00:08:28,354
Chaganti Bala Subramanya Manohar

126
00:08:28,355 --> 00:08:29,105
And you?

127
00:08:29,771 --> 00:08:30,480
Dulla Ravi, sir

128
00:08:30,980 --> 00:08:31,438
Dula

129
00:08:31,938 --> 00:08:32,646
Dulla

130
00:08:33,396 --> 00:08:33,730
Dula

131
00:08:34,521 --> 00:08:35,145
Dulle

132
00:08:35,146 --> 00:08:36,355
You...

133
00:08:36,563 --> 00:08:36,938
What's now?

134
00:08:37,521 --> 00:08:38,605
Someone smashed your shop?
- Sir, sir

135
00:08:38,771 --> 00:08:39,062
Yeah?

136
00:08:39,063 --> 00:08:40,813
It's not a shop, sir... It's a company

137
00:08:41,188 --> 00:08:43,395
Find out who did it
and get us compensation, sir

138
00:08:43,396 --> 00:08:43,895
Ah...

139
00:08:43,896 --> 00:08:44,521
Anything else you want?

140
00:08:44,730 --> 00:08:45,313
You...

141
00:08:45,563 --> 00:08:46,605
First information

142
00:08:47,063 --> 00:08:48,313
then the compensation

143
00:08:48,438 --> 00:08:49,855
My head is going to burst

144
00:08:50,896 --> 00:08:53,771
To ease this headache,
I need a coffee or a good story

145
00:08:53,980 --> 00:08:54,896
Tell me a good story

146
00:08:55,188 --> 00:08:56,896
We come to file a case,
and you ask for a story?

147
00:08:57,021 --> 00:08:57,855
Just tell me

148
00:08:58,188 --> 00:08:59,021
Okay, we'll tell you, sir

149
00:08:59,230 --> 00:09:00,395
Which story do you want to hear?

150
00:09:00,396 --> 00:09:02,688
Your story...
You three are friends, right?

151
00:09:03,146 --> 00:09:03,563
Yes, sir

152
00:09:03,896 --> 00:09:04,645
Since intermediate

153
00:09:04,646 --> 00:09:05,688
And then?

154
00:09:06,188 --> 00:09:07,355
We did BA together, sir

155
00:09:07,855 --> 00:09:08,979
I wanted to start a business

156
00:09:08,980 --> 00:09:11,105
and he pursued photography
- He stayed just like that, sir

157
00:09:11,438 --> 00:09:12,438
Not me, sir... Him

158
00:09:12,730 --> 00:09:13,563
I'm an introvert, sir

159
00:09:14,480 --> 00:09:16,813
Looking at you guys,
I can tell you're a bunch of crazy fellows

160
00:09:17,563 --> 00:09:19,271
Your enemy must have smashed your company

161
00:09:20,063 --> 00:09:20,771
What's up with you, Dula?

162
00:09:21,355 --> 00:09:22,938
Sir, I'm allergic to enemies

163
00:09:23,146 --> 00:09:25,521
If someone talks harshly,
I go cry in a corner

164
00:09:26,271 --> 00:09:27,938
I never fight with anyone

165
00:09:28,271 --> 00:09:28,771
Hmm

166
00:09:29,063 --> 00:09:30,396
What about you, chatterbox?

167
00:09:33,146 --> 00:09:33,730
Sir

168
00:09:34,063 --> 00:09:35,855
2 months and 13 days ago

169
00:09:36,271 --> 00:09:39,313
in the middle of the road,
someone hurled filthy abuses at me

170
00:09:39,521 --> 00:09:41,480
You must have done
something to provoke him

171
00:09:41,938 --> 00:09:42,688
Please hear me out completely, sir

172
00:09:44,355 --> 00:09:46,271
It was during my days working in a DOPIDO

173
00:09:47,896 --> 00:09:48,980
[Phone Rings]

174
00:09:51,771 --> 00:09:52,105
Hello

175
00:09:52,313 --> 00:09:53,979
Good morning, Mr. Gali Parameshwara Rao

176
00:09:53,980 --> 00:09:56,146
We are calling from the
Dopedo Complaint Division

177
00:09:56,438 --> 00:09:57,355
Complaint division, huh?

178
00:09:58,021 --> 00:09:58,646
Then listen,

179
00:09:59,105 --> 00:10:01,895
install mobile toilets
for our Dopedo bikes

180
00:10:01,896 --> 00:10:03,520
It's hard to relieve ourselves
anywhere just like that.

181
00:10:03,521 --> 00:10:04,646
There are CC cameras, you know

182
00:10:04,771 --> 00:10:06,520
Also, lighters for
cigarettes along the way

183
00:10:06,521 --> 00:10:09,563
Sir, sir, sir... We are calling
to talk about the complaints against you.

184
00:10:09,730 --> 00:10:10,230
Against me

185
00:10:10,563 --> 00:10:11,355
Who complained?

186
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:13,646
Sir, it's reported that
you are smoking during the ride

187
00:10:13,896 --> 00:10:15,646
Just trying to be friendly
with the customer, So what...

188
00:10:15,980 --> 00:10:18,771
And also, you've been verbally
abusing customers as you please

189
00:10:19,063 --> 00:10:20,270
Who said that? Is that black guy,

190
00:10:20,271 --> 00:10:22,145
who rode three days ago
and cheated me out of ten rupees

191
00:10:22,146 --> 00:10:23,813
If I find that rascal...

192
00:10:24,021 --> 00:10:25,230
Why so much anger, sir?

193
00:10:25,438 --> 00:10:27,187
If you speak politely with customers,

194
00:10:27,188 --> 00:10:29,480
you'll get a good rating,
and your incentives will increase

195
00:10:29,688 --> 00:10:29,980
You mean...?

196
00:10:30,355 --> 00:10:31,980
You'll get extra income, sir

197
00:10:32,230 --> 00:10:32,855
Extra income?

198
00:10:33,021 --> 00:10:33,646
How much?

199
00:10:33,896 --> 00:10:36,021
About two to three thousand rupees

200
00:10:38,855 --> 00:10:40,188
Two to three thousand a day means...?

201
00:10:40,646 --> 00:10:41,896
Please hang up the call right now

202
00:10:42,230 --> 00:10:43,230
You should have told me this earlier

203
00:10:43,521 --> 00:10:46,020
From now on, you'll see me
as the most courteous driver ever

204
00:10:46,021 --> 00:10:47,145
Haha... Bye!

205
00:10:47,146 --> 00:10:48,230
Bye, sir. Thank you

206
00:10:48,355 --> 00:10:49,938
I can drink every day with
two to three thousand - [Phone chimes]

207
00:10:53,313 --> 00:10:54,645
The customer is my king!

208
00:10:54,646 --> 00:10:55,688
I'm coming

209
00:10:56,771 --> 00:10:58,230
Why hasn't he come yet?

210
00:10:58,396 --> 00:11:00,355
On TV, they say,
they will arrive instantly

211
00:11:01,813 --> 00:11:03,355
Hey... um...
Hey, stop...

212
00:11:03,521 --> 00:11:04,438
stop...

213
00:11:04,730 --> 00:11:05,688
Take those fish and step aside

214
00:11:05,855 --> 00:11:06,605
What?

215
00:11:06,730 --> 00:11:08,895
Do I look like someone who sells fish?

216
00:11:08,896 --> 00:11:09,354
So?

217
00:11:09,355 --> 00:11:11,146
I booked you
- Me?

218
00:11:11,438 --> 00:11:13,521
Check if you want, 1965

219
00:11:13,771 --> 00:11:14,646
What, were you born then?

220
00:11:14,855 --> 00:11:16,688
Not born, man... OTT

221
00:11:17,021 --> 00:11:19,230
OTT? Is it an OTP?
Yeah...

222
00:11:19,980 --> 00:11:20,395
Correct, sir

223
00:11:20,396 --> 00:11:20,937
Yeah

224
00:11:20,938 --> 00:11:22,813
Please, sir. Take your seat, sir

225
00:11:22,980 --> 00:11:24,521
Oh boy, he knows English too

226
00:11:24,688 --> 00:11:25,855
- Welcome DOPEDO, sir.
- Okay

227
00:11:26,146 --> 00:11:26,730
hold this

228
00:11:27,855 --> 00:11:29,480
What's with the attitude?

229
00:11:29,688 --> 00:11:30,521
No, sir

230
00:11:30,813 --> 00:11:32,105
It's a 5-star rating job

231
00:11:32,438 --> 00:11:33,896
Here, give those watery flowers

232
00:11:34,271 --> 00:11:36,396
Sir, sir, sir...
please take your seat, sir

233
00:11:36,855 --> 00:11:38,562
Don't feel bad... they're fresh fish

234
00:11:38,563 --> 00:11:40,063
The hell with 5-star rating

235
00:11:40,563 --> 00:11:42,937
Sir, will you pay with cash or PhonePe?

236
00:11:42,938 --> 00:11:45,563
I'll give you a fish. Take
it home and ask your wife to make curry

237
00:11:45,855 --> 00:11:47,896
Sir... I'm not married yet

238
00:11:48,188 --> 00:11:49,730
So there's no power in your body, huh?

239
00:11:50,980 --> 00:11:52,646
You're quite the joker, sir

240
00:11:53,355 --> 00:11:54,854
Are you laughing or crying?

241
00:11:54,855 --> 00:11:56,813
Be careful, otherwise we both will die

242
00:11:57,688 --> 00:11:59,146
Maybe this is why they give incentives

243
00:11:59,438 --> 00:12:00,563
Hey, stop... stop

244
00:12:00,771 --> 00:12:01,188
Stop

245
00:12:01,355 --> 00:12:01,896
For what, sir?

246
00:12:02,146 --> 00:12:03,771
There my fish will getting on

247
00:12:04,271 --> 00:12:04,771
Fish?

248
00:12:04,896 --> 00:12:05,980
Yeah, my wife

249
00:12:06,188 --> 00:12:06,855
Stop, man!

250
00:12:07,896 --> 00:12:08,812
They have free buses, right, sir?

251
00:12:08,813 --> 00:12:11,146
Can't you stop where I tell you to stop?
You dirty crab

252
00:12:11,855 --> 00:12:12,563
Come on now

253
00:12:13,063 --> 00:12:15,188
you're walking like a prawn... Get on!
Move

254
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:17,771
Sir, sir, sir... only one person per ride,
sir It's okay, let's adjust

255
00:12:17,896 --> 00:12:18,895
You can't do that, sir

256
00:12:18,896 --> 00:12:20,396
She knows that way only

257
00:12:20,605 --> 00:12:21,896
The fishes are drying out

258
00:12:22,063 --> 00:12:23,230
You hold the waist

259
00:12:23,396 --> 00:12:23,730
Mine?

260
00:12:23,855 --> 00:12:24,895
Not yours, mine

261
00:12:24,896 --> 00:12:26,438
Just an idea, come on

262
00:12:29,063 --> 00:12:30,730
Hey, not this way, we have to go that way

263
00:12:31,021 --> 00:12:31,895
One-way, sir. We can't go there

264
00:12:31,896 --> 00:12:33,646
It's okay, the SI is our guy

265
00:12:33,813 --> 00:12:35,563
If we go this way, we can go fast

266
00:12:35,730 --> 00:12:37,313
Can't you understand. Just go...

267
00:12:37,438 --> 00:12:40,021
go... go... right, right

268
00:12:40,396 --> 00:12:41,396
Hey, stop

269
00:12:41,730 --> 00:12:42,605
For what, sir?

270
00:12:42,813 --> 00:12:44,230
My small fish is here.

271
00:12:44,438 --> 00:12:45,146
Small fish?

272
00:12:45,521 --> 00:12:47,646
Yes, he is my son. stop!

273
00:12:47,896 --> 00:12:48,438
I can't sir.

274
00:12:48,646 --> 00:12:50,313
I can't means how? Stop.

275
00:12:50,521 --> 00:12:51,896
It's a bike, sir, not a lorry

276
00:12:52,105 --> 00:12:52,896
Stop, man

